  </sharedSelectionEntries>
  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="Battlesuits" id="8797-8fec-3f62-3b7f" hidden="false" publicationId="733a-d454-80f2-c90e">
      <description>Every T'au battlesuit of the Infantry unit type (Commanders, the battlesuit characters, and Crisis, Stealth, XV9 Hazard and Broadside battlesuits) has the Heavy and Mechanised sub-types, using the official 2.0 Mechanised rules. They may fire all their weapons in each Shooting Attack, including Heavy and Ordnance weapons after moving, and may still charge; Poisoned and Fleshbane wounds against them must be re-rolled, but Armourbane weapons re-roll failed To Wound rolls against them; Haywire, Detonation and Battlesmith affect them as Dreadnoughts; and no model that is not Mechanised may join their unit.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Drone" id="abcb-0f0a-21ea-938f" hidden="false" publicationId="733a-d454-80f2-c90e">
      <description>Models with the Drone sub-type represent semi-autonomous mechanical constructs designed to accompany and assist sentient operators on the battlefield. A model with the Drone sub-type follows these rules: - Controlled Protocol: If all non-Drone models in the parent unit are destroyed, any remaining models with the Drone sub-type in that unit are immediately removed from play as casualties. - Cybernetic Cohort: Drones may be taken as their own units, or purchased as upgrades for a parent unit with the Drone Controller special rule. Drones taken as upgrades are treated as additional models within that squad. When allocating hits to the unit, wounds may be allocated to any Drone model using its own Toughness and Save characteristics. - Inbuilt Protocols: All models with the Drone sub-type possess Jet Packs and the Defender special rule. - Networked Morale: Models with this sub-type ignore their own Leadership characteristic. Instead, they always use the highest Leadership characteristic available in their parent unit for all Morale checks, Pinning tests, and Regroup tests. A unit made up only of Drones uses its own Leadership. - Objective Denial: Models with this sub-type can never control objectives, but they can deny (contest) objectives controlled by the enemy.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Auxiliaries" id="e027-81a6-2a4f-749c" hidden="false" publicationId="733a-d454-80f2-c90e">
      <description>Kroot and Vespid fight for the Greater Good, but not as T'au. They do not gain Sept (X) traits, never benefit from Ethereal Invocations, and may not use Supporting Fire. Kroot units have Move Through Cover and Infiltrate unless their entry says otherwise.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Drone Controller" id="c521-c1b6-bf08-26db" hidden="false" publicationId="733a-d454-80f2-c90e">
      <description>A unit with this special rule may include models with the Drone sub-type, either as part of its Unit Composition or bought from its Options, up to the number its datasheet allows. These drones follow the Drone (sub-type) rules for drones taken as part of a parent unit.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Jet Packs" id="cec5-f1a0-ee98-0e56" hidden="false" publicationId="733a-d454-80f2-c90e">
      <description>T'au battlesuits, drones and hover drones use the official 2.0 Jet Pack rules. Vespid use Vespid Wings instead (see Wargear). A unit entirely equipped with jet packs may increase its Movement Characteristic by 6, move over friendly and enemy models and units, and ignore terrain while moving in the Movement phase (Dangerous Terrain tests still apply when beginning or ending a move in it, and Difficult Terrain counts as Dangerous). After it has finished shooting in the Shooting phase, it may make an additional 6" move in the same way, whatever weapons it fired. During any Reaction that lets it move, the move is increased by 6". Models with jet packs gain Bulky (2), or Bulky (3) if they already have Bulky (2), and Deep Strike. T'au battlesuits do not gain Bulky this way; they use the Bulky value on their datasheet instead.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Markerlights" id="055e-aced-4c7e-9337" hidden="false" publicationId="733a-d454-80f2-c90e">
      <description>When a model fires a markerlight, each hit places one Markerlight token on the target unit instead of causing damage. Tokens last until the end of the turn. Before another friendly unit shoots at the marked unit, it may spend tokens as follows (each token once): A seeker missile may instead spend one token to fire at Ballistic Skill 5, without line of sight to the target.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Saviour Protocols" id="e16a-d6c3-1a81-796f" hidden="false" publicationId="733a-d454-80f2-c90e">
      <description>When a wound is allocated to a friendly T'au character or battlesuit within 3" of a friendly Drone, you may roll a D6; on a 2+, that wound is allocated to the Drone instead (use the Drone's save)†.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Sept (X)" id="de79-d017-7909-4d83" hidden="false" publicationId="733a-d454-80f2-c90e">
      <description>When building an army, choose one Sept for each detachment. Every T'au unit in that detachment (not Auxiliaries) gains Sept (X), where X is the chosen Sept. Commander Farsight and his Bodyguard may only join a Farsight Enclaves detachment; Commander Shadowsun, Aun'Va and Longstrike may only join a T'au Sept detachment. Other Unique characters may join any Sept.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Drone Support" id="674a-b1a0-56b7-c85b" hidden="false" publicationId="733a-d454-80f2-c90e">
      <description>A unit that may take drones lists how many in its Options. Drones taken this way are models in that unit: they move and shoot with it and are counted for its Morale checks. If the rest of the unit is destroyed, any remaining drones are removed as casualties.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Drone Units" id="90c6-0407-8d2c-a51c" hidden="false" publicationId="733a-d454-80f2-c90e">
      <description>Drones taken as their own unit (Tactical Drones, Sniper Drone Team, Heavy Gun Drones) use these profiles as normal and gain the Sept (X) of their detachment.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Expendable" id="11c0-41d9-34ff-92b9" hidden="false" publicationId="733a-d454-80f2-c90e">
      <description>Drones never hold or contest objectives†, and destroying a drone does not count as destroying a model for Morale, Warlord Traits or victory conditions.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Unit Type" id="1243-8d02-4d8c-2223" hidden="false" publicationId="733a-d454-80f2-c90e">
      <description>Drones are Infantry with jet packs and the Drone sub-type†. A Drone may never be a character or join another unit.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Invulnerable Save (X)" id="a806-8312-c10a-6b19" hidden="false" publicationId="733a-d454-80f2-c90e">
      <description>The model has an Invulnerable Save of X, which may be taken against any Wound instead of its armour save.</description>
    </rule>
